In article <4017@pikes.Colorado.EDU> lngo@pikes.Colorado.EDU (Linh D. Ngo) writes:

>Is a multi-player version of Nethack available in the near-future? It seems
>the next logical progression of Nethack would be multi-user interaction
>much like that of MUD (Multi-User Dungeon). 

>Of course, this would require a rather major rewrite. Purist Nethackers
>would no doubt object. The computing requirements may press hard on certain
>CPUs...  But it can't be that tough, can it? How about a modem link for
>two personal computers?

As I see it, the problem is not the rewrite or CPU power. The REAL PROBLEM
is time used in the dungeon.

A) Players take turns to play.
   - Playing becomes too slow because you have to wait for all others to act.

B) Playing is done in real time.
   - This changes nethack into an action game. You could no longer play
     strategically. Just hit everything in sight.

If someone has a solution, I can't see any obstacle in creating this game.
